# Python — the hooks and their suite under .claude/ are scripts, not a package.
__pycache__/

# Index SQLite is machine-local. The skill, .mcp.json and .codeindexignore
# are shared so Claude in this clone uses the same map.
.claude/cache/codebase-index/

# Session state, already ignored by a nested `.gitignore` holding `*` — but
# git reads those at any depth and the code index reads only the root files
# its config names, so without these two lines it indexed both trees whole,
# session logs included: text from PR comments, reviews and sweeps came back
# ranked beside code as repository evidence. #53 owns the measurement, which
# moves with the checkout; `.claude/scripts/test_root_ignore_coverage.py` is
# the gate. blueprint-backend and blueprint-admin list .remember/ the same way.
.remember/
.superpowers/

# The native generated trees, which are the same divergence from the other
# direction. `android/.gitignore` and `ios/.gitignore` are Capacitor's own
# templates; git reads them at any depth and the code index reads neither, so
# everything `cap sync` and Gradle write under them was indexed whole.
# Measured 2026-09-21: 90 of 342 indexed files and 7,980 of 9,185 symbols were
# the two copied web bundles, and a minified `main-*.js` outranked the source
# for two of eight ordinary questions. Four of these lines were
# `.codeindexignore`'s until now — the root file is where the gate wants them,
# because it is the one both tools read.
#
# This list is what those templates generate in a checkout that has built, not
# a mirror of everything they could. `test_root_ignore_coverage.py` is what
# catches the next one, and it asserts these paths whether or not the checkout
# has built, so the lock holds on CI's clean tree too.
/android/.gradle/
/android/build/
/android/app/build/
/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
/ios/App/build/
/ios/App/output/
/ios/App/Pods/
/ios/App/App/public/
/ios/DerivedData/
/ios/capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins/

# The generated files beside them, which the block above missed and its own
# verification could not have caught: that check rebuilt the native trees from
# the list it was checking, so it compared the list with itself. These come
# from walking a checkout that has really run `cap sync` and asking which of
# its nested-hidden paths the root file does not reach — the method, not the
# answer, is the part worth keeping.
#
# Three of them sit in directories holding tracked files, so no directory is
# wholly hidden and `test_root_ignore_coverage.py` can never report them: its
# subject is a directory, and a generated file beside a tracked one is invisible
# to it. The regression lock names these individually for that reason.
# `local.properties` also carries an absolute SDK path from whichever machine
# ran the build.
/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
/android/app/src/main/res/xml/config.xml
/android/local.properties
/ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json
/ios/App/App/config.xml

# /review-branch's proof that it ran, which grok-review.sh requires before it
# reads a missing suggestions.md as a clean pass. Ignored so that a standalone
# review does not dirty the tree the same helper refuses to review over.
/.grok-review-ran

# /pr's description, written at the checkout root because gh-pr-create.sh
# publishes no other path, and removed by that helper once the PR is open.
/pr-body.md
/pr-title.txt

# The user's local task list, kept current by Claude (CLAUDE.md, Working in
# this repo). Local by design: it changes too often to go through a PR.
/TODO.md
